{
 "comment": "Pinned test-data sources for the benchmark harness. Each source is downloaded once into the cache, checked against sha256, and only members matching the patterns of a kind are extracted. 'vm_split': member paths are Debian system paths (same layout as the Ubuntu VM that built the primers), so members in the VM's training half (tools/corpora.py) are dropped. Licenses are SPDX ids; test data is only measured, never used to build primers or minds. Dropped after measuring primer overlap (fetch.py --calibrate): botocore (median 45%), lodash (up to 90%), tango SVGs (median 27%). 'group': sources that count as one when balancing bytes (the three Kodak photos).",
